WEBVTT

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:06.780
<i>Our team, the Fuurin Academy middle school
baseball team, made it to the district finals.</i>

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:03.890
<b>Oobi</b>

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:03.890
<b>Oobi</b>

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:03.890
<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:03.890
<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:05.850
<b>Mayumura</b>

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.520
<b>Mayumura</b>

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.720
<i>There we met Oobi Middle's team,
who count a certain Mayumura Michiru-chan</i>

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.670
<i>and three elite ex-Yokohama Little
players among their ranks.</i>

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.370
<i>The third inning.</i>

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:22.540
<i>Despite a good start, our starting 
pitcher, Nishina, quickly flagged,</i>

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.910
<i>and due to some follow-up errors,
 we gave away five runs...</i>

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.710
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.710
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.710
<b>Oobi</b>

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.930
<i>...handing them a giant lead.</i>

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:31.920
Three outs! Change sides!

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.720
<i>We hadn't managed
a single hit in four innings,</i>

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.150
<i>but thanks to everybody's determination,</i>

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:45.480
<i>Kandori and Chisato's RBI hits 
netted us two runs.</i>

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.820
<i>After that, Oobi Middle's ace,
Mayumura Michiru,</i>

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.940
<i>got up on the mound in
 the middle of the fifth,</i>

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:56.740
<i>and the game turned into
a pitchers' duel between her</i>

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:59.160
<i>and our unexpected
volunteer reliever, Sawa-san.</i>

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.330
<i>The score stayed at 5-2 as
we entered the final inning.</i>

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.330
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.330
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.330
<b>Oobi</b>

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.250
Foul!

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:09.780
Foul!

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:13.240
Mutsuko! Keep us alive!

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:18.430
<i>A hair away from losing, Mutsuko
forced the other team into an error.</i>

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.990
<i>It's the top of the seventh,
two outs, runners on first and third.</i>

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:25.090
<i>We won't give up!</i>

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:29.160
<i>We're going to capitalize on this 
chance and turn this game around!</i>

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:05.990
<b>We've Come This Far</b>

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.450
By the skin of our teeth!

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:11.420
Two outs, with runners on first and third!

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.480
Lucky!

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:18.780
Y'know, other than those four seniors, 
Oobi Middle's not all that hot.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.220
Thank goodness!

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:23.320
Ya got this!

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:25.820
<i>Batting first, second base, Fujii-san.</i>

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:30.100
Get 'em, Chisato!

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:39.600
Keep it up! Keep it up!

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.050
Chisato!

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:46.330
<i>Fujii won't hit a home run,
but we should ditch going high.</i>

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.290
Ball.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.500
Rude!

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.950
Ya got this! Ya got this!

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.610
Ball! Ball four!

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.680
All right! Chisato's on base!

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:11.520
Bases loaded!

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:15.320
Tanba-san, take over for me by the base.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.760
I'm up next.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:17.980
R-Right!

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.550
One big last job for you, huh?

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:22.970
I'm counting on you, Tao.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:24.960
Yeah...

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.290
I'll let you have the honor of cleaning it up.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:37.710
<i>I don't believe this.</i>

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.300
<i>What is it with these girls?</i>

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:44.430
All right!

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:45.880
It went through!

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:49.090
5-3!

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.730
Keep going, keep going!

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:57.480
<i>My legs... I can't....</i>

00:04:58.890 --> 00:04:59.730
Mutsuko?!

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:10.500
Safe!

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.650
Hell yeah!

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:14.250
Nice one, Tao!

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:16.600
Right?!

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.790
Just one run in it!

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.540
With runners on second and third!

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:24.920
Mutsuko?!

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.260
Wh-What's wrong?! Are you okay?!

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:29.600
I-I'm fine!

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:32.070
My left leg just cramped up a little.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:34.680
It'll probably be fine in a bit.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:37.320
Senpai!

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.180
I don't believe this.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:51.720
In rubber-ball, even the boys
haven't gotten good hits on my pitches.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.730
What is it with these girls?

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:56.460
Why does this team have all these girls?

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:55.920
Hey, Michiru!

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:56.460
Hey!

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:57.510
Hey!

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:01.380
Pull yourself together, Michiru!
They haven't caught up yet!

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:03.670
First base is open.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:07.840
Sawa's too dangerous, so just walk her
and face off against Shigeno.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:09.660
Huh? Why should I?!

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:12.300
I promise I'll get her out! Let me take her on!

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.100
Michiru!

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:15.850
You need to calm down.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.230
If you don't agree to it,
I'll put Seko in instead.

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:20.460
Is that what you want?

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:22.660
Fine.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.990
<i>Batting third, pitcher, Sawa-san.</i>

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.710
Wrap it up, Yayoi!

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:35.750
Walkin' her?!

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.660
They want a showdown with Daigo?

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.590
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.590
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.590
<b>Oobi</b>

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:43.590
Ball four!

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:50.510
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.130
Aren't you up next?

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:08.010
Foul!

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:12.700
Ya got this! Ya got this!

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:15.490
Ball!

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:18.540
Strike!

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:30.300
<i>Wait, that's...</i>

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:32.460
<i>Mr. Shigeno?!</i>

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:38.810
<i>My idol...</i>

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.770
<i>My ideal pitcher!</i>

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:46.420
<i>A daring left-handed 
overhand pitch like yours...</i>

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:52.030
<i>Michiru, don't tell me you're...</i>

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:58.490
<i>That's the secret weapon we're saving
for the toughest teams at Regionals.</i>

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:01.210
<i>We don't have that luxury anymore.</i>

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:04.210
<i>We're already facing
a tough team here and now!</i>

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:07.380
<i>An overhand pitch?</i>

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.170
Ball!

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:14.640
<i>Did you see that?</i>

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.890
<i>This is my real fastball!</i>

00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:20.310
I-It's so fast...

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:23.440
She still had an overhand
like that up her sleeve?

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:26.740
<i>That was her ace in the hole
back in Touto Boys, too.</i>

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:28.400
<i>That overhand pitch...</i>

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:30.560
<i>So you've been saving it until now.</i>

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:34.360
<i>That's some next-level power, 
compared to the sidearm.</i>

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.320
<i>But...</i>

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:38.030
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:38.030
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:38.030
<b>Oobi</b>

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.740
<i>We just need one run to tie.</i>

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.500
<i>If I don't do something now, it's game over!</i>

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:44.460
<i>He didn't see it missing the zone.
He just couldn't swing.</i>

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.390
<i>Finish this, Michiru.</i>

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:49.340
<i>There's no way he can hit that pitch!</i>

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:53.420
Foul!

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:55.170
<i>He got his bat on it?!</i>

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:04.340
<i>I have to believe in the work I've put in.</i>

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:24.020
<i>I have to, for everyone who's followed me
this far and believed in me as their captain!</i>

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:38.630
Nice, Daigo!

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:40.050
You got this!

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:41.600
Good luck!

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:46.850
Foul!

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:51.710
<i>Not bad, Shigeno Junior.</i>

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:53.780
Don't give up, Michiru!

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:55.240
Your pitches are on fire!

00:09:58.220 --> 00:09:59.150
<i>That's right.</i>

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:03.130
<i>Back then, my hopes and dreams were dashed.</i>

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:06.340
<i>My passion for baseball
was almost snuffed out.</i>

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:09.670
Ball!

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:14.540
Foul!

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.750
Keep it up, Michiru!

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:26.440
<i>They brought me back from the edge.</i>

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:32.490
<i>They even quit Senior to keep my dream alive.</i>

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.400
<i>I know...</i>

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:41.530
<i>I know this will be the only time
I get to play with and against the guys!</i>

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:47.450
<i>That's why I want to use this chance
and get to the very top... with this team!</i>

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:58.970
Yes!

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.430
It went through!

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:04.350
We're tied!

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:05.840
Back home!

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:13.770
Safe!

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:20.680
We took the lead!

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:24.070
Nice one, Daigo!

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:34.980
Hell yeah! Awesome!

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:37.560
This is incredible! They took the lead!

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:40.170
This is crazy! Are they seriously
gonna go to Regionals?

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:45.640
Wow, Daigo's come a heck of
a long way since his Dolphins days.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:49.390
Who would've ever thought he'd hit one
of Mayumura Michiru's crazy fastballs?

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:52.600
Must be your DNA, Kaoru-chan.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.080
Yeah, no.

00:11:55.760 --> 00:12:02.690
I keep texting the source of the baseball DNA,
but he refuses to read his messages.

00:12:03.850 --> 00:12:04.490
Huh?

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:06.280
Hey, Shigeno!

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:07.840
Over here, over here!

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:14.430
Hey, what's Fujii doing with my wife?!

00:12:14.430 --> 00:12:16.630
Don't tell me you got together while I was away...

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:17.780
You dumbass!

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:24.800
<b>Fuurin
Academy</b>

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:24.800
<b>Fuurin
Academy</b>

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:24.800
<b>Fujii</b>

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:24.800
<b>Sagara</b>

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:24.800
<b>Sawa</b>

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:24.800
<b>Shigeno</b>

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:24.800
<b>Nishina</b>

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:24.800
<b>Kabashima</b>

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:24.800
<b>Tanba</b>

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:24.800
<b>Kandori</b>

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:21.230
He's here cheering his own daughter on!

00:12:21.230 --> 00:12:22.710
Chisato-chan, the leadoff.

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:23.930
Oh, really?

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:24.800
Yup, really.

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:28.740
By the way, why are you sitting so far back?

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:32.770
Because Daigo didn't want me to come,
so I don't want him to see me.

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:37.230
He said this tourney was just a trial run,
so it wasn't important enough to watch.

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:39.150
A trial run, huh?

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.650
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.650
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.650
<b>Oobi</b>

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:42.650
It's one hell of a game for a "trial run."

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:45.810
Strike!

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:47.390
Three outs. Change sides.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:50.630
All right, let's keep our lead and win this!

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:52.900
All right!

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:58.460
Mutsuko, is your leg all right?

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:00.210
Yup, it's fine.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:02.330
I'd go out there even if I had to crawl.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:05.050
If we make it through this inning,
we're going to Regionals!

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:07.810
Come on, let's take our positions.

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:21.910
<i>Bottom of the seventh, Oobi Middle to bat.</i>

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:26.050
<i>Batting eighth, center field, Yamamuro-kun.</i>

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:27.570
Michiru!

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:29.900
Keep your head up!

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:31.550
It's not over yet!

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:40.810
Nice!

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:44.400
<i>Batting ninth, left field, Kouda-kun.</i>

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:46.930
<i>Those are good pitches
you're throwing, Yayoi.</i>

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:50.390
<i>I hope we can get to the end like this.</i>

00:13:58.250 --> 00:13:58.950
Out!

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:00.150
Nice one, Chisato!

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:01.400
Two outs!

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:06.880
Huh. Unlike her father, who was a sieve
 on second, the daughter's actually good.

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:10.320
I'm in a good mood, so I'll let that go.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.120
Just one more out!

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:16.000
<i>Batting first, second base, Idemitsu-kun.</i>

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.580
Get on base, Idemitsu!

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:18.180
<i>Just one more out.</i>

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:19.590
<i>One more out...</i>

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:21.170
<i>...and we're off to Regionals.</i>

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:22.540
<i>This is nuts.</i>

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:30.550
Hit by pitch!

00:14:30.860 --> 00:14:31.940
Yes! He's on base!

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:35.270
<i>Batting second, pitcher, Mayumura-san.</i>

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:37.730
Oh, whoops! My bad.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:42.950
You know, I just noticed 
something pretty extraordinary.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:43.470
Hm?

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:43.940
Huh?

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.440
This Mayumura girl...

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:48.630
Is she <i>that</i> Mayumura's daughter?!

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.390
Are you for real?

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:52.040
Of course she is.

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:54.500
This is the older twin, Michiru-chan.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:56.650
She's been over to our house a couple of times.

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:57.910
Seriously?!

00:14:58.220 --> 00:15:01.450
Well, I guess that explains her nice form.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:04.970
Yeah, guess so.

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:09.290
But you know, the pitcher she really 
looks up to isn't Mayumura-kun,

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:12.050
but someone by the name of Shigeno Goro.

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:13.240
Huh?

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:18.680
Ball!

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:21.410
Good! Keep your eye on the ball, Michiru!

00:15:21.410 --> 00:15:23.150
Their pitcher's losing it!

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:25.610
Yayoi, keep it up!

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:28.090
<i>She hasn't pitched in a long time.</i>

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:30.820
<i>It's only natural she'd start
flagging in her third inning.</i>

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:32.530
<i>Just one more out needed.</i>

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:34.280
<i>Come on, Sawa-san!</i>

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:35.740
Strike!

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:38.440
Good!

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:42.670
<i>She missed two sliders,
so she got a strike with a fastball.</i>

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:44.680
Come on, Michiru!

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:55.100
<i>They sacrificed playing in Senior to play
middle school rubber-ball with me.</i>

00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:58.060
<i>I won't...</i>

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:02.770
<i>...let another girl get in our way!</i>

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.030
Nishina!

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:10.900
Run!

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:15.090
Back home!

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.750
Safe!

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:21.960
Yeah!

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:23.520
We caught up!

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:25.150
Timeout.

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:31.630
<i>She had time to make it to third on that
close play, but she stopped on second?</i>

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:34.840
Wow, that girl's really good.

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:38.310
She waited for a fastball and hit it plumb.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:39.860
The next hit's game over.

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:43.810
Let's walk the next batter and duke it out
 with their cleanup. It'll be easier to defend.

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:46.160
Face off against Uozumi, huh?

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:49.770
That's another kind of dangerous,
but it might be better.

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:51.080
Yayoi!

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:56.450
Yayoi, you're done.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:17:00.710
You can't control your breaking balls, 
and your fastballs aren't sharp, either.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:03.860
You should really stop now,

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:07.140
before it ends up like that time in Little
when you couldn't pitch anymore!

00:17:07.140 --> 00:17:09.270
Like that time in Little?

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:11.220
What?

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:13.300
<i>Ah. The cat's out the bag.</i>

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:17.260
So when you said you hadn't
pitched in a while, you meant...

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:21.680
While pitching for Little,

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:25.890
Yayoi hurt her elbow and the doctor 
banned her from pitching altogether.

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:28.600
Oh no...

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:30.110
So what now?

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:34.440
You gonna switch me with Nishina, who hasn't
warmed up, at this make-or-break moment?

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:41.100
My elbow's completely healed since then.

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:42.850
The doctor confirmed it as well.

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:43.540
Huh?

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:46.910
It's healed a lot in one year.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:49.520
I'd say it's fine now.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.290
You can even pitch again.

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:55.390
But just make sure you don't overdo it.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:58.980
There is still a chance you could reinjure it.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.640
I'm sorry. I should have told you.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:04.460
But still!

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:06.540
I'm telling you, it's fine.

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:09.520
You guys think elbow pain is just
a minor inconvenience, don't you?

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:13.230
If it was really hurting,
I wouldn't even be able to pitch.

00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:16.150
So it really healed up?

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:19.700
I just don't want to see 
you like that ever again.

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:22.610
Sawa-san...

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:25.290
You're not supposed to make a face like that.

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:28.390
I'm fine. I just got a little tired.

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:29.800
Let's kick it up a notch!

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:32.250
We've come this far, so let's go win it, captain!

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:38.800
Yayoi...

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:03.530
Okay!

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:09.980
Ball four.

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:14.250
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Uozumi-kun.</i>

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:18.840
<i>Michiru, you...</i>

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.140
<i>You get it, right?</i>

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:25.180
<i>I stopped at second
so they had to face you head-on.</i>

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:27.180
You have to finish this, Uozumi!

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:28.700
Walk us off!

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:37.240
Nice one, Daigo!

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:38.750
He did well to stop that!

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:41.700
Daigo's seriously gotten a whole lot better.

00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:46.580
In Dolphins, he was basically a total
beginner with zero motivation.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:53.370
Me and Kaoru-chan were saying earlier
how amazing the Shigeno Goro DNA is.

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:56.960
Ball!

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:00.210
I'm not so sure about that.

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:04.340
It wouldn't be fair on him
to say it's all in his genes.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:08.190
He's been training like crazy this past year.

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:14.120
You know I went to play in the
Shikoku League as a player-coach, right?

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:14.940
Sure.

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:19.150
I've played Major League, and NPB...
in Taiwan, and Central America...

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:21.970
All the time, I just wanted to play.

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:24.780
But when retirement finally
reared its head last year,

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:30.260
the only reason I even considered a second
career as a coach was all thanks to him.

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:30.950
Huh?

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:32.620
Foul!

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:37.750
Did you know that most of the second-years
 got kicked off Fuurin's team last year

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:39.960
due to a shoplifting incident?

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:41.770
What? Seriously?!

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:44.120
The coach felt responsible,

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:48.810
so he resigned and the club 
was put on a half-year hiatus.

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:53.760
Up until then, the team had been strong.
Our daughter, Izumi, played for them too.

00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:58.020
Then, all of a sudden, the first-years 
didn't have any older players or even a coach.

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:59.270
Are you kidding me?!

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:01.780
Chisato didn't tell me about any of that!

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:04.180
She might not even know herself.

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:04.990
Ball.

00:21:05.280 --> 00:21:08.410
Around that time, I was
also pretty directionless.

00:21:08.980 --> 00:21:12.280
Pop... Please teach me baseball!

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:17.390
I'd never seen him looking
 so determined before.

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:26.950
Foul!

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:28.970
Nice!

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:29.910
Come on!

00:21:29.910 --> 00:21:31.310
You got this!

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:33.240
Sawa-senpai, go!

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.600
Let's do this!

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:42.260
Hang in there, Yayoi!

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:45.450
<i>I wasn't planning on trying this hard.</i>

00:21:46.730 --> 00:21:48.200
<i>But I can't help it!</i>

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:50.990
<i>It's a forkball!</i>

00:21:56.730 --> 00:21:58.000
Foul! Foul!

00:21:58.000 --> 00:21:58.890
Aw man!

00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:00.810
At first, I turned him down.

00:22:00.810 --> 00:22:01.500
Huh?

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:04.460
But he was so serious.

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:08.370
<i>If I try hard enough,
and I get everyone's help,</i>

00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:12.350
<i>I think the Fuurin baseball team can
crawl out of this dark hole we're in.</i>

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:24.520
Mutsuko!

00:24:01.210 --> 00:24:03.420
This one play's going to decide it all.

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:06.180
Whether we win and go to Regionals,
and then on to Nationals!

00:24:06.180 --> 00:24:11.550
You know, Daigo, it's good to be enthusiastic,
but you should let us have weekends off.

00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:14.320
You'll never toughen up with that attitude!

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:16.290
I want us to go even higher!

00:24:16.290 --> 00:24:19.020
Were you even listening to me?!

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:20.960
Next time: "Nice Game!"

00:24:19.470 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>Nice Game!</b>

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:23.290
Run to the stage of your dreams!
